§ `k062 -- Jake's underpayment claim`

#ASSERT `May the Magistrates Court hear my claim` `Jake's underpayment claim` EQUALS `yes: under the Commonwealth law that confers it, which s 9 does not itself name`

#ASSERT `Who may constitute the Court for my case` `Jake's underpayment claim` EQUALS `one magistrate (s 7(1))`

#ASSERT `May the Court sit there for my case` `Jake's underpayment claim`

#ASSERT NOT `Do the Supreme Court rules of evidence apply to my case` `Jake's underpayment claim`

#ASSERT `Must the Court explain cross-examination to me` `Jake's underpayment claim`

#ASSERT `Can I get this from the record of my case` `a written judgment, its reasons, or a written order` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes, as of right on request (s 33(3))`

§ `ss 9, 10 -- may the Court hear my claim`

#ASSERT `May the Magistrates Court hear my claim` `a contract debt within the civil limits` EQUALS `yes: under the Magistrates Court (Civil Proceedings) Act 2004, as s 10 says`
#ASSERT `May the Magistrates Court hear my claim` `a contract debt the Civil Proceedings Act does not reach` EQUALS `no: the law my claim rests on does not give the Court jurisdiction over it`
#ASSERT `May the Magistrates Court hear my claim` `a claim under a WA Act that confers it` EQUALS `yes: under the written law that confers the jurisdiction, as s 9 says`
#ASSERT `May the Magistrates Court hear my claim` `a claim with no law behind it` EQUALS `no: the Court has only the jurisdiction that a law confers on it (s 9)`

§ `s 7 -- who will hear my case`

#ASSERT `Who may constitute the Court for my case` `a claim under a WA Act that confers it` EQUALS `the Court as constituted in the way the other written law requires (s 7(4))`
#ASSERT `Who may constitute the Court for my case` `the same claim, at an adjournment` EQUALS `one magistrate (s 7(1))`
#ASSERT `Who may constitute the Court for my case` `a claim where JPs are allowed` EQUALS `one magistrate, or one or more JPs, as the regulations or another written law allow (s 7(2))`

#ASSERT `What does the bench of JPs decide` 2 1 TRUE EQUALS `decided in my favour by the majority (s 7(6)(b))`
#ASSERT `What does the bench of JPs decide` 1 1 TRUE EQUALS `adjourned to a place and date the JPs decide, the JPs being equally divided (s 7(6)(b))`
#ASSERT `What does the bench of JPs decide` 2 1 FALSE EQUALS `no valid decision: every JP must be present throughout (s 7(6)(a))`
#ASSERT `What does the bench of JPs decide` 1 0 TRUE EQUALS `s 7(6) does not apply: a single JP decides alone`

§ `s 8 -- where my case may be heard`

#ASSERT `May the Court sit there for my case` `a sitting in another State, approved and allowed`
#ASSERT NOT `May the Court sit there for my case` `a sitting in another State, approved but not allowed there`

§ `s 14 -- rules of evidence`

#ASSERT `Do the Supreme Court rules of evidence apply to my case` `a contract debt within the civil limits`

§ `s 17 -- a refused claim`

#ASSERT `May I lodge my refused claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `May I lodge my refused claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE

§ `ss 28, 29 -- registrars`

#ASSERT NOT `May a registrar take this step in my case` `entering final judgment on my claim after trial`
#ASSERT `May a registrar take this step in my case` `another step that the rules of court delegate to a registrar`

#ASSERT `How many days to appeal a registrar's decision`  EQUALS 21

#ASSERT `Can I appeal the registrar's decision` TRUE 21 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Can I appeal the registrar's decision` TRUE 22 FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal the registrar's decision` TRUE 40 TRUE

§ `s 23 -- correcting a judgment`

#ASSERT `May the Court correct my judgment` `a material arithmetic error`
#ASSERT NOT `May the Court correct my judgment` `a wrong decision on the facts or the law`

§ `s 33 -- the record`

#ASSERT `Can I get this from the record of my case` `the transcript of the electronic recording of the hearing` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `only with the Court's leave (s 33(4))`
#ASSERT `Can I get this from the record of my case` `the record of proceedings made by the magistrate or JPs` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, as of right on request (s 33(3))`
#ASSERT `Can I get this from the record of my case` `a written judgment, its reasons, or a written order` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `only with leave, which the Court must give unless it has good reason not to (s 33(8))`

§ `s 16(4) -- contempt`

#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for contempt`  EQUALS 12000

